`parse_filesize` passes each test string to `lookup_unit_table(..., strict=False)`. That function matches `(?P<num>...)\s*(?P<unit>...)\b`, returns early only if the unit pattern does not match, and otherwise sets `num = float(m.group('num').replace(',', '.'))`. Every one of the 18 test inputs uses a supported unit, so all 18 calls reach the `num` assignment. Taking just the numeric prefixes from the suite gives values from `0.001` up to `99999`, so the observed range is min `0.001` and max `99999.0`, with 18 observations.

